{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>From you.</b> It is postponed, and likewise is \"a man from you who brings an offering\" (Leviticus 1:2), and there are many like it. Or it may be: \"from you\" — from your property. Or \"from you\" may be a hint to exclude stolen property, for so it is written: \"one who hates robbery\" (Isaiah 61:8)." "<b>From the animal.</b> \"An offering\" is the general category, and afterward \"from the cattle\" and \"from the flock\" — which are the species of sheep and goat — the specifics. Also the word \"your offering\" is a general category."], :book :leviticus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {0 "Resolved עול׳ as עולם by context, though it may abbreviate עולה; the Isaiah citation supports עולם."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:08:26.965862790Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}